# The CFRG draft's first worked relation: knowledge of a discrete
# logarithm.  Our driver reads this one, and the rest of the
# published suite, straight out of the test vectors at runtime; this
# file is the same relation written by hand so it can be checked
# without them.
secrets x
claims  x
eq  X   G

# An instance: one distinct generator per base name, so the
# environment is faithful and the verdict above transfers to it.
# The exponents are ours and carry no meaning; every element of a
# prime-order group is a generator power, so this is simply a way
# to write distinct elements down.
point G  2
